AUDIO: 'are linked in the description if you\'d like to use them for your own videos. And this time, we\'ll give Claude the same clip, but we\'ll also attach our style document for the street interview edit. On this second attempt, Claude does something completely different. It'

[03:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'opens on her best line before the question\'s even asked. So, instead of a slow setup, we hook the viewer with the payoff first. The dead pauses are gone, too. And it even brands the interviewee as stranger one on entry, using that signature street interview label'

[03:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'straight from our style document. Plus, Claude didn\'t ask us a single question this time. It just knew because we\'d already taught it. That\'s the difference between telling an AI model what to do and teaching it how you work. But one clean edit is easy. The real'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'test is whether the same trick works on a completely different style. So, let\'s give it something that looks nothing like the last video. We\'ll go with the talking head style. Someone speaking to camera while captions pop up with b-roll cutting in on the words that matter.'

[03:59] [scene:talk]
